In Phase 1, we built a working backend with MongoDB, Mongoose, CRUD, Zod validation, standardized responses, error handling, API versioning and Swagger.
Now we'll move beyond making APIs work and focus on making the backend maintainable, scalable, secure and production-oriented.

In Phase 2, we'll improve the architecture before adding authentication and AI features


Phase 2 roadmap:

Step	        Topic	                    What we'll build
2.1	            Backend architecture	    Understand and refine layered architecture
2.2	            Environment configuration	Centralized configuration and validation
2.3	            Database engineering	    Connection lifecycle, indexes and schema design
2.4	            Service layer	            Business logic and repository responsibilities
2.5	            Error architecture	        Custom errors and centralized error handling
2.6	            Security foundations	    Helmet, CORS, rate limiting and sanitization
2.7	            Logging	                    Structured logs and request tracking
2.8	            API quality	                Pagination, filtering and sorting improvements


